This is my first ever post to the Nethack newsgroup,  although I have been
playing for a couple years.  So I obviously think the game is very
clever,  and the dev team did a good job in most respects.

But what gives with the way spells are learned/cast/etc.?!!  IMO this
part of the game was the most obviously lacking in 3.0,  and is
unfortunately still shitty.

I have many complaints/suggestions,  but for now I would like to
suggest getting rid of the possibility of being teleported and
paralyzed simultaneously when trying to read a spellbook.  

My Preist had saved his spellbooks until he was level 12,  wisdom 18,
intelligence 14,  with maximium luck.  He was locked in a room,
standing on "Elbereth" 
engraved by a wand of digging.  Upon reading a uncursed spellbook he
was simultaneously teleported and paralysed,  and of course I got to
hit the spacebar 50-60 times and watch him die at the hands of a few
relatively harmless monsters.  And this isn't the first time this has
happened. 

How am I supposed to safely read spellbooks?  Requiring 18 wis,  18
int,  max luck and blessing every spellbook seems to be the only way
to avoid instant death.  What was the dev team thinking?

Ted Pederson


